s `ht` to `fr-HT` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/get-locale.ts:7-18`).\n\n**Main formatting path.** `formatDate` (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-utils/src/dates/date-util.ts:306-372`):\n- Resolves the locale and calendar, and sets `noToday` to true automatically for Amharic (`am`) (lines 307-316).\n- Checks `dayjs(date).isToday()` (line 327). If the date is today and `noToday` is false, it uses `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat(locale, { numeric: 'auto' })` with `format(0, 'day')`, which yields the localised \"today\", then uppercases the first letter (lines 328-332).\n- Otherwise it formats with `Intl.DateTimeFormat`. English uses `en-GB` so dates don't show AM/PM. English and Amharic standard mode join parts with hyphens, and wide mode uses \" — \" (lines 333-350).\n- Ethiopic calendar output drops the era (lines 352-364).\n- It appends `, <time>` when `time === true`, or when `time === 'for today'` and the date is today (lines 368-370).\n\n**Time and datetime helpers.** `formatTime` uses `toLocaleTimeString(getLocale())` with 2-digit hour and minute (`date-util.ts:396-401`). `formatDatetime` calls `formatDate` with `time: true` (`date-util.ts:416-418`).\n\n**Partial dates.** `formatPartialDate` parses a partial string, fills the missing year, month or day into the options, then delegates to `formatDate` (`date-util.ts:241-280`).\n\n**Defaults and options.** `FormatDateOptions` is at `date-util.ts:172-206` and `defaultOptions` at lines 208-215 (`mode: 'standard'`, `time: 'for today'`, `noToday: false`). Calendar lookup is in `getDefaultCalendar` (`date-util.ts:164-168`).\n\n**Documentation.** The generated API docs describe the same behaviour: \"If the date is today then 'Today' is produced (in the locale language). This behavior can be disabled with `noToday: true`\" (`openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/formatDate.md:9-25`). The same wording appears in `formatPartialDate.md:20` and in `FormatDateOptions.md:69`.\